Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 08/27/2023]
1.  Ecm = 215 and 403 keV: from Powell et al. 1998, 1999; these values were determined independent of stoichiometries and stopping powers. Strength for the Ecm = 215 keV
    resonance agrees with Zhang et al. 2021 and Limata et al. 2010.
2.  Ecm = 792 keV: weighted average of Trautvetter 1975 and Engel et al. 2005.
3.  Ecm > 1 MeV: weighted average from Tab. 1 in Trautvetter 1975 and Endt & van der Leun 1973, after both of these sets were renormalized using strength of 792
    keV resonance.
4.  Upper limits have been disregarded: (i) wg < 4e-5 eV for Ecm = 450 keV from Powell et al. 1999; (ii) wg < 0.001 eV for Ecm 2246 keV from Endt & van der Leun 1973.
5.  Direct capture estimated from potential model using experimental spectroscopic factors from (3He,d) and mirror (d,p) reaction.


